    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Panama's Role in the World</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> The Importance of Panama in Global Trade</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Evaluate spoken information from radio or television. Interactive: Engage in role-play scenarios to resolve everyday conflicts.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can comprehend and evaluate information from a news broadcast on a local issue (e.g., "After evaluating the news broadcast, it's clear that the proposed improvements to the Panama Canal's infrastructure are designed to ease congestion and enhance global trade efficiency.")
Can role-play resolving a disagreement over environmental concerns vs. economic growth (e.g., "What would you say if a classmate suggested prioritizing development over sustainability?")
Can use questions to confirm understanding of key ideas in media broadcasts (e.g., "Why did the speaker mention increased funding for infrastructure improvements around the Panama Canal?").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 30%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 20%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher begins by projecting a world map showing major shipping routes and highlighting the Panama Canal. Students are asked to share what they know or speculate about the Canal's importance. The teacher then plays a very short, silent video clip (15-20 seconds) of large ships transiting the Canal. Students are prompted to describe what they see and how it might relate to "global trade" and "shipping." Core vocabulary such as "Panama Canal," "shipping," "trade," and "routes" are elicited and written on the board.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models the pronunciation of key vocabulary words crucial for understanding the theme. Words like "global," "trade," "efficiency," "congestion," "infrastructure," "investments," "environmental," and "impact" are pronounced clearly. Special attention is given to the long vowel sound /oʊ/ as in "global" and "local," and the alternation of full and reduced vowels in multisyllabic words like "environmental" /ɪnˌvaɪ.rənˈmen.təl/ and "impactful" /ɪmˈpækt.fəl/. Students are encouraged to repeat chorally and individually.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of new vocabulary using concept-checking questions and examples.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">For "congestion": "If there is heavy congestion on a highway, can cars move quickly or slowly?" (Slowly). "Is congestion a problem for efficiency?" (Yes).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">For "efficiency": "If a process is efficient, does it waste a lot of time and resources, or does it save them?" (It saves them). "Do shipping companies want efficient routes?" (Yes).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] [Time]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Panama's Role in the World."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Students will listen to an authentic news broadcast audio (approx. 2-3 minutes) titled "Panama Canal's Future: Balancing Global Trade and Environmental Concerns." The material is an informative news report, formal in register, and targets B1.2 comprehension. It includes instances of passive voice (e.g., "The Canal has been managed by the Panama Canal Authority since 1999."), Present Perfect Continuous (e.g., "The Canal has been improving global trade..."), and mentions of "investments," "environmental groups," and "efficiency."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening: Receptive: Evaluate spoken information from radio or television.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Listening (First listen):</b> Students listen for the main idea. "What are the two main topics discussed in this news broadcast about the Panama Canal?" (Global trade benefits and environmental concerns).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Detailed Listening (Second listen with worksheet):</b> Students complete a True/False activity based on specific information from the broadcast.</li>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The Panama Canal Authority has been managing the Canal for over 50 years." (False, since 1999).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Increased investments in infrastructure are expected to reduce shipping delays." (True).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Environmental groups have raised concerns about the Canal's impact on local ecosystems." (True).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Global trade would have faced significant challenges if the Canal had not been built." (True, an example of a third conditional concept).</li>
                    </ul>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] [Time]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Listening.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice identifying and comprehending target grammar (passive voice, present perfect continuous, second/third conditionals) and vocabulary (e.g., *operation, traffic, congestion, efficiency, investments, environmental groups*) while discussing the Canal's impact and expressing hypothetical ideas.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice: Listen and Fill-in-the-Blanks (Passive Voice / Present Perfect Continuous):</b> The teacher plays specific short excerpts from the news broadcast. Students listen carefully and fill in missing words in sentences provided on a worksheet. The focus is on identifying passive voice and present perfect continuous structures.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 1: "Since 1999, the Panama Canal _______ (manage) by the ACP." (Answer: has been managed)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 2: "The increasing traffic _______ (cause) some congestion in recent years." (Answer: has been causing)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example 3: "New investments in infrastructure _______ (announce) to enhance efficiency." (Answer: have been announced)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-Controlled Practice: Listen and Rephrase (Vocabulary / Conditionals):</b> The teacher plays sentences from the broadcast that imply hypothetical situations or use target vocabulary. Students listen and then work in pairs to rephrase the sentences using target vocabulary or conditional structures, ensuring they maintain the meaning.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher plays: "If the Canal didn't exist, transport of goods would be much longer and more expensive." Students rephrase using 'faced challenges' or 'global trade.' (E.g., "Global trade would face significant challenges if the Canal didn't exist.")</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher plays: "The Canal has made a big difference to how things move around the world." Students rephrase using 'impacted global trade.' (E.g., "The Canal has been impacting global trade for decades.")</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction: Clarifying Information:</b> In pairs, students receive a list of statements related to the broadcast, some correct and some incorrect. They listen to the broadcast again (or specific sections) and discuss which statements are true or false, justifying their answers to their partner. They are encouraged to use questions to confirm understanding, such as "Why did the speaker mention increased funding for infrastructure?" or "Are you sure about that point on environmental concerns?" This promotes interactive listening and the use of specific trade-related terms appropriately.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] [Time]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Panama's Role in the World."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format: Role-Play - "Panama Canal Future Discussion"</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will engage in a role-play simulating a community meeting or panel discussion about a proposed new "Green Investment Project" for the Panama Canal, which aims to further enhance its efficiency but also addresses environmental sustainability. Each student will adopt a specific role:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Panama Canal Authority Representative:</b> Focus on economic benefits, investments, efficiency, and future plans.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Environmental Activist:</b> Raise concerns about ecosystems, sustainable practices, and long-term environmental impact.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Local Business Owner:</b> Focus on local economy, job creation, and potential impact on small businesses.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Global Shipping Company Manager:</b> Discuss costs, delays, routes, and global trade efficiency.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will listen to each other's perspectives and evaluate the information presented. They must use the target vocabulary (e.g., *investments, environmental groups, congestion, efficiency, influence*) and grammatical structures (passive voice, second/third conditionals to express hypothetical ideas, present perfect continuous to describe ongoing impacts) to make their points, ask questions to clarify understanding, and attempt to resolve disagreements over environmental concerns vs. economic growth. For example, "If we invested more in green technology, global ecosystems wouldn't be as affected," or "The Canal has been supporting global commerce, but also causing environmental concerns."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] [Time]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation using a checklist/rubric during the role-play to assess students' listening comprehension, ability to evaluate spoken information, and interactive skills.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students' active participation in the "Panama Canal Future Discussion" role-play. The teacher observes their ability to listen to different viewpoints, respond appropriately, ask clarifying questions (e.g., "Why did the speaker mention increased funding for infrastructure improvements?"), and integrate learned vocabulary and grammar.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Listening Comprehension:</b> Accurately responds to partners' points, demonstrates understanding of different perspectives.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Vocabulary:</b> Effectively employs words like *congestion, efficiency, investments, environmental groups, global relationships*.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Grammar:</b> Appropriate use of passive voice, second/third conditionals, and present perfect continuous.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> Intelligible pronunciation, particularly of /oʊ/ sounds and reduced vowels in multisyllabic words.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Interaction & Collaboration:</b> Actively listens, asks relevant questions to confirm understanding, and engages respectfully with opposing viewpoints.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a short exit ticket with the following prompts:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new piece of information you learned about the Panama Canal's impact on global trade or environment today from listening to your classmates?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How effectively did you listen to and understand your partner's perspective during the role-play, especially when there was a disagreement?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] [Time]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How has listening to different viewpoints on the Canal's impact changed your own understanding of its role in global trade and environmental issues?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What strategies did you use today to better understand complex information in the audio broadcast and during the role-play? What could you improve for next time?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">"The students demonstrated good initial comprehension of the news broadcast's main ideas and effectively participated in the controlled practice. The role-play was successful in encouraging interactive listening and the use of target vocabulary and grammar, particularly when discussing hypothetical situations with conditionals. However, some students struggled to formulate spontaneous questions to confirm understanding during the pair work and role-play. For the next lesson, I will provide more explicit sentence starters for asking clarifying questions and allocate more time for peer feedback on listening strategies."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">"Today, we focused on listening to and evaluating information about the Panama Canal's impact. Next lesson (Lesson 2: Reading Comprehension), we will delve deeper into these topics by reading an article that provides more detailed economic and environmental arguments, reinforcing the vocabulary and concepts introduced today in a different skill context."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date] [Time]</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>